1. Free personal use
Individuals may use, copy, and modify this Skill free of charge for their own
non-commercial activities, including personal learning, private photo editing,
and sharing their personal, non-commercial photographs.

2. Commercial use requires permission
Any commercial use requires prior written permission from the copyright holder.
Commercial use includes use in business or organizational operations, paid
photo-editing services, client work, advertising, monetized content, and inclusion
in a paid product, service, application, plugin, course, or template collection.
This applies to the original Skill and modified versions. No commercial rights
are granted automatically by downloading, modifying, or installing this Skill.

3. Non-commercial redistribution
Non-commercial sharing of the Skill and modified versions is permitted only
with this license and existing copyright notices intact. Modified versions must
clearly indicate that they have been modified and remain subject to this license.
Recipients must receive no fewer restrictions than those stated here.

4. Photographs and outputs
This license covers the Skill's instructions, prompts, and included resources.
It does not transfer ownership of users' photographs or grant rights to any
third-party material. Commercial use of this Skill to produce outputs still
requires the permission described in section 2. Separate terms of the image
generation or editing service continue to apply.

5. Warranty and termination
The Skill is provided "AS IS", without warranties, to the extent permitted by
applicable law. To the extent permitted by law, the copyright holder is not liable
for damages arising from its use. The permissions granted by this license end
if its conditions are violated.

6. Commercial authorization
Contact the copyright holder through the official GitHub repository to request
commercial authorization. Written permission must state the permitted scope.

